---
import MainLayout from "../../layouts/MainLayout.astro";

const title = "West Covina City Hall Updates | StayJustin";
const description =
  "West Covina City Hall news, council meeting updates, budget questions, Fire Station 3 coverage, overtime spending, lawsuits, censure issues, and local government decisions explained simply.";
---

<MainLayout
  title={title}
  description={description}
  canonical="https://www.stayjustin.com/city-hall/"
>
  <section class="section">
  <div class="container">
    <article class="content hub-page">
      <p class="page-kicker">West Covina City Hall</p>
      <h1>City Hall Decisions Residents Should Watch</h1>

      <div class="summary-box">
        <p>
          West Covina is dealing with emergency repairs, rising overtime,
          labor agreements, and budget pressure — all at the same time.
        </p>
      </div>
  
<section class="section">
  <div class="container">
    <article class="content hub-page">
      <p class="page-kicker">West Covina City Hall</p>
      <h1>City Hall Decisions Residents Should Watch</h1>

      <div class="summary-box">
        <p>
          West Covina is dealing with emergency repairs, rising overtime,
          labor agreements, and budget pressure — all at the same time.
        </p>
      </div>
    
<section class="section">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="section-header clean-header">
      <div>
        <h2 class="section-title">Latest City Hall Coverage</h2>
        <p class="section-sub">
          These are the key issues currently affecting West Covina.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="story-grid">

      <article class="story-card">
        <span class="story-tag">Fire Department</span>
        <h3>
          <a href="/city-hall/fire-station-3-emergency-repairs-continue/">
            Fire Station 3 emergency repairs continue under special authority
          </a>
        </h3>
        <p>
          The city is continuing emergency authorization due to a rodent infestation,
          allowing work without the normal competitive bidding process.
        </p>
        <a class="read-more-link" href="/city-hall/fire-station-3-emergency-repairs-continue/">
          Read full breakdown →
        </a>
      </article>

      <article class="story-card">
        <span class="story-tag">Overtime</span>
        <h3>
          <a href="/city-hall/west-covina-overtime-spending-analysis/">
            Overtime spending is already over 50% at mid-year
          </a>
        </h3>
        <p>
          Police and fire overtime are already past the halfway mark, raising
          questions about whether reductions later in the year are realistic.
        </p>
        <a class="read-more-link" href="/city-hall/west-covina-overtime-spending-analysis/">
          See the numbers →
        </a>
      </article>

      <article class="story-card">
        <span class="story-tag">Budget</span>
        <h3>
          <a href="/city-hall/west-covina-mid-year-financial-report-breakdown/">
            Mid-year financial report shows spending outpacing revenue
          </a>
        </h3>
        <p>
          The city reports a mid-year gap between spending and revenue, with
          explanations tied to timing — but pressure still exists.
        </p>
        <a class="read-more-link" href="/city-hall/west-covina-mid-year-financial-report-breakdown/">
          Review the report →
        </a>
      </article>

      <article class="story-card">
        <span class="story-tag">Labor</span>
        <h3>
          <a href="/city-hall/west-covina-fire-management-mou-costs/">
            Fire Management agreement adds long-term costs
          </a>
        </h3>
        <p>
          A new labor agreement introduces salary and benefit changes that will
          affect future budgets beyond the current year.
        </p>
        <a class="read-more-link" href="/city-hall/west-covina-fire-management-mou-costs/">
          Understand the impact →
        </a>
      </article>

      <article class="story-card">
        <span class="story-tag">Full Analysis</span>
        <h3>
          <a href="/city-hall/april-21-2026-city-council-budget-questions/">
            Budget questions residents should be asking right now
          </a>
        </h3>
        <p>
          A full breakdown connecting emergency spending, overtime, labor costs,
          and budget assumptions into one bigger picture.
        </p>
        <a class="read-more-link" href="/city-hall/april-21-2026-city-council-budget-questions/">
          Read full analysis →
        </a>
      </article>

    </div>
  </div>
</section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container intro-block">
      <p class="section-sub">Latest City Hall coverage</p>
      <h2 class="section-title">
        Budget Questions Residents Should Watch
      </h2>
      <p class="intro-copy">
        The latest council packet includes Fire Station 3 emergency repairs,
        a new fire management agreement, overtime spending concerns, and a
        mid-year financial report showing spending moving faster than revenue.
      </p>
      <p class="intro-copy">
        <a href="/city-hall/april-21-2026-city-council-budget-questions/">
          Read the full April 21 budget questions breakdown
        </a>
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container intro-block">
      <h2 class="section-title">What Matters Right Now</h2>
      <p class="section-sub">
        The main City Hall stories shaping West Covina right now.
      </p>

      <div class="story-grid">
        <article class="story-card">
          <span class="tag">Fire Station 3</span>
          <h3>
            <a href="/city-hall/fire-station-3-emergency-repairs-continue/">
              Fire Station 3 emergency repairs continue
            </a>
          </h3>
          <p>
            West Covina is being asked to continue emergency authority after
            rodent infestation repairs triggered bypassing the normal bid process.
          </p>
        </article>

        <article class="story-card">
          <span class="tag">Overtime</span>
          <h3>
            <a href="/city-hall/west-covina-overtime-spending-analysis/">
              Overtime spending is already over 50% at mid-year
            </a>
          </h3>
          <p>
            Police and fire overtime are the numbers residents should watch as
            the city moves through the second half of the fiscal year.
          </p>
        </article>

        <article class="story-card">
          <span class="tag">Budget</span>
          <h3>
            <a href="/city-hall/west-covina-q2-financial-report-2025-26/">
              West Covina Q2 financial report explained
            </a>
          </h3>
          <p>
            The mid-year report shows revenue and expenditures moving at very
            different speeds. Here is what that means.
          </p>
        </article>

        <article class="story-card">
          <span class="tag">Fire Department</span>
          <h3>
            <a href="/city-hall/west-covina-fire-management-mou-2024-2028/">
              Fire Management MOU: what it costs over time
            </a>
          </h3>
          <p>
            A new agreement with fire management adds future costs and changes
            related to compensation, benefits, and staffing language.
          </p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container intro-block">
      <h2 class="section-title">Follow the City Hall Story</h2>
      <p class="section-sub">
